  "description": "Commuter action abounds along the bustling 4-track West Coast Main Line in Train Sim World®. Dash through the complex layout of London Euston aboard the hard-working Class 350 and embark across the Northwest corner of the Capital to Milton Keynes, with expresses and stoppers alike.\n\nBritain’s busiest and oldest inter-city railway into London, the West Coast Main Line, stretches northward out of the brutalist hub of Euston and plays host to over 30 million passengers a year. This monster mainline runs at capacity all hours of the day, with fast and slow lines offering local and longer-distance commuter destinations.\n\nAccelerating through the dense boroughs of Camden and Brent, the WCML is accompanied by further passenger and freight action. The Bakerloo line surfaces at Queens Park, and shares tracks with the Lioness line. At the massive complex of yards near Wembley, Southern join into the fray with their unique cross-London, dual-voltage commuter service."
